is</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Adaptive control of odor-guided locomotion: behavioral flexibility as an antidote to environmental unpredictability.</article-title><source>Adapt Behav</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>217</fpage><lpage>253</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003678-Deodhar1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Deodhar</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kupfermann</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Studies of neuromodulation of oscillatory systems in <italic>Aplysia</italic>, by means of genetic algorithms.</article-title><source>Adapt Behav</source><volume>8</volume><fpage>267</fpage><lpage>296</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003678-AharonovBarki1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aharonov-Barki</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Beker</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruppin</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Emergence of memory-driven command neurons in evolved artificial agents.</article-title><source>Neur Comput</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>691</fpage><lpage>716</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003678-Ruppin1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ruppin</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Evolutionary autonomous agents: a neuroscience perspective.</article-title><source>Nat Rev Neurosci</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>132</fpage><lpage>141</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11836521</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003678-Nepomnyashchikh1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-